Playwright reference

If you would like to annotate your tests with something more substantial than a tag, you can do that when declaring a test. Annotations have a type and a description for more context and are available in reporter API. Playwright's built-in HTML reporter shows all annotations, except those where type starts with _ symbol. 

For example, to annotate a test with an issue url:

test(defineChecksumTest(
   "Verify the banner and modal pop-up based on region",
   "r0pdL"
 ), {
 annotation: {
   type: 'bug',
   description: 'User is able to complete a question without an assignee',
 },
}, async ({ page }) => {
 // ...
});

Any test annotation will show up within the Checksum playwright report, making it easier for both engineers and customers to quickly understand, or remember, the details of a bug.


