Alternatively, using right-of/left-of selectors
Playwright provides pseudo-classes to select elements based on their layout relative to others:
:left-of(selector): Selects elements to the left of the specified selector.


:right-of(selector): Selects elements to the right of the specified selector.


:above(selector): Selects elements above the specified selector.


:below(selector): Selects elements below the specified selector.


:near(selector): Selects elements near (within 50 pixels of) the specified selector.


await page.locator('input[type="text"]:below(:text("Test Users"))').first()


In-general, using .first() is not best practice, but in this scenario it makes the most sense since we want the closest input element below the targeted text.

