Tips to being a stronger QA developer
Optimize Test Runs
Use --grep-invert "@bug" to skip known failing tests and focus on passing tests first. Revisit bug-related tests afterward.
Streamline Debugging
Comment out unnecessary test code to speed up execution. For example, if a test checks sorting in ascending and descending order and one works while the other fails, temporarily disable the passing check to focus on the failure.
Compare Test Reports Efficiently
Compare the latest failure report with a previous successful run to pinpoint issues instead of reviewing every line manually.
Use Efficient Locator Strategies
Utilize the Pick Locator button to accurately grab locators for elements.
Take advantage of the Recording feature to generate assertions via the UI.
Optimize Assertion Timeouts
Reduce the global assertion timeout when debugging to get faster feedback on failures.
Run CI Tests Locally Before Dispatch
Execute CI=true locally before running tests from dispatch to ensure a quicker test cycle.

